# Third-party packages. The workspace root grows a node_modules/ from wrangler
# and vitest runs, and it was never ignored here (only the sub-repos ignore it),
# so a broad `git add` swept two cache files into history on 2026-07-28 —
# including a wrangler account-id cache. Regenerated on demand; never committed.
node_modules/

# Cloned repos (managed by setup.sh)
youcoded/
# ...and as a SYMLINK. `youcoded/` with a trailing slash matches a directory only,
# so a symlink of the same name slipped past it and reached master on 2026-08-28
# (a workspace worktree has no sub-repo clones, and one was linked in to run the rig).
youcoded
youcoded-core/
youcoded-admin/
wecoded-themes/
wecoded-marketplace/
# ...and the same slashless lines for the other four. The 2026-08-28 incident
# (see docs/PITFALLS.md -> Worktrees) only ever got a slashless `youcoded`, so a
# worktree that symlinks ANY other sub-repo could still commit the link — and a
# merge will overwrite the real clone with it, because git happily clobbers a
# path it considers ignored. Verified 2026-08-31: all four showed as untracked
# in a workspace worktree with the sub-repos linked in.
youcoded-core
youcoded-admin
wecoded-themes
wecoded-marketplace
# The roadmap-check test fixture carries a FAKE `youcoded/` sub-repo (one .ts file its
# claim anchor points at). The slashless `youcoded` above matches at any depth, so
# without this re-include the fixture silently never reached CI — PR #11's first run
# failed on exactly that (98 green locally, 2 red in CI).
!scripts/fixtures/roadmap/youcoded

# Worktrees and temp directories
.worktrees/
*-worktree*/
*-unified/
*-phase*/
*-decoupling/
*-sessions/

# Skill runtime state (brainstorming/writing-plans session dirs etc).
# Contain ephemeral working notes from skill invocations and don't carry
# value across machines.
.superpowers/

# Ad-hoc scratch dir occasionally used for files we don't want to track.
# If something proves useful, promote it to scripts/ or docs/.
scratch/

# Auto-title artifacts
.auto-title
.auto-title-audit.tmp

# Claude project config
# Track: commands/, hooks/, rules/, skills/, settings.json (shared across machines)
# Ignore: settings.local.json (user/machine-specific), worktrees/
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
.youcoded/

# Worktree container dirs (per-repo .wt convention)
*.wt/
scratch-*/
# The workspace-level worktree container (CLAUDE.md convention: worktrees/<name>).
# Each entry is its own git checkout — committing them embeds foreign repos.
worktrees/
# Downloaded release/beta installers used for VM install testing — large
# binaries that must never enter git history.
beta/

# Full event-stream transcripts from the harness review runner
# (youcoded/desktop/test-engine/review-harness.mjs). A transcript is a
# debugging artifact for the session that produced it, not durable history —
# five models' full event streams would dominate this repo's diff history.
# The reviews themselves (appended into the investigation doc) are the
# durable record.
docs/active/investigations/harness-review-runs/
docs/active/investigations/conversation-triage-runs/
# Same reasoning for the model EVALUATOR (youcoded/desktop/test-engine/
# harness-eval.mjs): each cell writes its full conversation and its grades
# beside the run, and those are not durable history.
#
# The difference from the two runners above: this runner's durable artifact —
# report.md — lives INSIDE the ignored directory. So the pattern is written in
# three parts rather than one, because git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent DIRECTORY is excluded: ignore the contents (`/**`), re-include the
# directories themselves so git can descend into them, then re-include exactly
# the reports. Without this, committing a report would need `git add -f` every
# time and the first forgotten one loses the record of a paid run.
docs/active/investigations/harness-eval-runs/**
!docs/active/investigations/harness-eval-runs/**/
# Reports are named report-<plan>.md so two experiments on the same day cannot
# overwrite each other (2026-08-13: one silently destroyed another's report).
# The glob MUST stay wildcarded — a literal `report.md` here would silently
# ignore every per-plan report and undo that fix.
!docs/active/investigations/harness-eval-runs/*/report*.md

# UI-audit screenshot sheets (evidence for docs/active/design/2026-08-25-*); regenerate per the folder README
docs/active/design/*-ui-audit/images/

# Perf-lab screenshots. These are working files — five 1600x1000 PNGs per report,
# regenerated by every run and only ever consumed by compare.mjs's pixel diff against
# a sibling run's dir. The REPORTS themselves (perf-reports/*.json, *.md) and the
# curated review/ folder stay tracked: they are the durable record of what was measured.
# (scratch/ already covers the fixture HOME, the downloaded engine/model assets and
# the per-boot desktop.log copies.)
perf-reports/shots/
# Deck answers (*.answers.json) are Destin's decisions and are COMMITTED (feature-flow design §2).
# Throwaway decks live in scratch/, which is ignored above. `*.serve.json` is a runtime lock.
*.serve.json

# Python bytecode from the deck tooling + its tests
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Written beside a deck spec by review-cards.py serve (the workbench it boots for live panes)
*.workbench.log
